From 4bd5622ffa3db48282316f4609b44191c10381ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 08:32:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Receipt emails: ask the receiver to acknowledge, with a
 dashboard tile for the sender

The receipt email goes to whoever is now personally holding the items
(the "To" person, on a send or a receive alike) with a curated
acknowledgment line naming who handed the items over, and a single
one-click "Yes, I acknowledge" button. Clicking it opens a small page
that records the acknowledgment immediately on load - no second
"Confirm" step and no "No" option, so one click is the whole flow. (A
GET link recording state on load is unusual, and a link-prefetching
mail scanner could in theory open it first - accepted here in exchange
for the one-click-no-extra-page flow that was asked for.)

On a receive specifically, the person who handed the items over also
gets a copy of the same receipt email, with no acknowledgment ask
(that's only for whoever is now holding the items).

Two cases are sent with no acknowledgment ask at all: corrections (no
real "To" person taking custody), and a batch that is entirely a return
to stock (every item ends up back "In stock" - nobody is taking
personal custody of anything).

New: lib/acknowledgment.ts (create/find/record), lib/acknowledgment-text.ts
(wording shared by the email and the page), a new "acknowledgments" tab
in schema.ts and supabase/setup.sql (the user needs to run the added
CREATE TABLE block once in the Supabase SQL editor - not created
automatically).

Dashboard: "My dashboard" shows "Acknowledged: X of Y" for items the
signed-in person sent (action = check_out).

Note on the Store: acknowledgment rows are the first ones in this app
that get UPDATED after creation (answer/answered_at filled in later)
rather than only appended. Supabase's upsert blanks any column not in
the row you pass it, so lib/acknowledgment.ts always upserts the full
existing row, never a partial patch - documented there for whoever
touches it next.

